    {
      "id": "en.n6.class-66.t01",
      "en": "Good morning, everyone. My topic today is street photography.",
      "es": "Buenos días a todos. Mi tema de hoy es la fotografía callejera.",
      "explanationEs": "Topic es el tema de la charla. Saludar y decir el tema es lo habitual al empezar.",
      "segments": [
        "Good morning, everyone. My topic",
        "today is street photography."
      ],
      "audioText": "Good morning, everyone. My topic today is street photography.",
      "audioMode": "tts",
      "languageCode": "en",
      "patternId": "n6-speaking-to-an-audience-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "en.n6.class-66.t02",
      "en": "A good opening makes the audience want to listen.",
      "es": "Una buena apertura hace que el público quiera escuchar.",
      "explanationEs": "Opening: la primera parte de la charla. Audience es el público que escucha.",
      "segments": [
        "A good opening makes the",
        "audience want to listen."
      ],
      "audioText": "A good opening makes the audience want to listen.",
      "audioMode": "tts",
      "languageCode": "en",
      "patternId": "n6-speaking-to-an-audience-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "en.n6.class-66.t03",
      "en": "My first point is about light. Next, I will talk about the camera.",
      "es": "Mi primer punto trata de la luz. Después hablaré de la cámara.",
      "explanationEs": "Point es cada idea del desarrollo. First y next indican en qué punto estás.",
      "segments": [
        "My first point is about light. Next,",
        "I will talk about the camera."
      ],
      "audioText": "My first point is about light. Next, I will talk about the camera.",
      "audioMode": "tts",
      "languageCode": "en",
      "patternId": "n6-speaking-to-an-audience-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "en.n6.class-66.t04",
      "en": "To sum up, light matters more than an expensive camera. That is my conclusion.",
      "es": "Para resumir, la luz importa más que una cámara cara. Esa es mi conclusión.",
      "explanationEs": "To sum up abre el cierre. Conclusion es la idea final que se queda el público.",
      "segments": [
        "To sum up, light matters more than",
        "an expensive camera. That is my conclusion."
      ],
      "audioText": "To sum up, light matters more than an expensive camera. That is my conclusion.",
      "audioMode": "tts",
      "languageCode": "en",
      "patternId": "n6-speaking-to-an-audience-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "en.n6.class-66.t05",
      "en": "The speaker looks at the audience and says, \"Thank you for listening.\"",
      "es": "La oradora mira al público y dice: «Gracias por escuchar».",
      "explanationEs": "Speaker es quien habla. Thank you for listening es el cierre más habitual.",
      "segments": [
        "The speaker looks at the audience",
        "and says, \"Thank you for listening.\""
      ],
      "audioText": "The speaker looks at the audience and says, \"Thank you for listening.\"",
